 elevation:{title:'A connected downhill route',kind:'QINGLING / ELEVATION SURVEY',text:'Ridge: 18 m. Side gully: 10 m. Junction: 2 m. In this model water follows connected routes downhill. A large facility away from the route cannot intercept the flow.'},
 tracer:{title:'Follow a virtual tracer',kind:'QINGLING / TRACER EXPERIMENT',text:'14:10: release at the ridge after rain stops. 14:20: arrival at the foothill. 14:30: entry into the tributary. Rainfall ending is not the same as runoff arrival ending.'},
 camera:{title:'Ten minutes later',kind:'QINGLING / CAMERA COMPARISON',image:'qingling-camera',text:'Rain stopped uphill at 14:10. Upstream water still entered the junction at 14:20; ponding grew by 14:30. Blue water and timestamps are teaching overlays on the illustrated camera view.'},
